From: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: disable handover IRQ once handover is done

Handover is a one-shot lifecycle event: qcom_q6v5_prepare() arms the
interrupt, the first (and only meaningful) firing releases the proxy
votes, and qcom_q6v5_unprepare() disarms it. The SM8750 ADSP firmware
however re-latches its ready/handover smp2p bits on every sensor-island
wakeup, so with a sensor client streaming (SSC accel+gyro) the handover
interrupt re-fires ~5 times per second for the whole uptime and floods
the kernel log with "Handover signaled, but it already happened"
(observed: >1000 messages in 4 minutes, wrapping the dmesg ring).

Disable the interrupt from the handler once the handover has been
performed; qcom_q6v5_prepare() re-arms it for the next boot cycle of the
remote processor. Keep qcom_q6v5_unprepare() balanced by only disabling
the interrupt when the handover never fired, and turn the leftover
re-fire message into a ratelimited one as a safety net.

Signed-off-by: Anze <aanzdev@gmail.com>
---
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -78,7 +78,12 @@
  */
 int qcom_q6v5_unprepare(struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5)
 {
-	disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
+	/*
+	 * Balanced with the enable_irq() in qcom_q6v5_prepare(): once the
+	 * handover fired, its handler already disabled the interrupt.
+	 */
+	if (!q6v5->handover_issued)
+		disable_irq(q6v5->handover_irq);
 	q6v5_load_state_toggle(q6v5, false);
 
 	/* Disable interconnect vote, in case handover never happened */
@@ -165,7 +170,8 @@
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		dev_err_ratelimited(q6v5->dev,
+				    "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
@@ -176,6 +182,16 @@
 
 	q6v5->handover_issued = true;
 
+	/*
+	 * Handover is a one-shot lifecycle event, but some firmware (the
+	 * SM8750 ADSP) re-latches its ready/handover smp2p bits on every
+	 * sensor-island wakeup, re-firing this interrupt several times per
+	 * second for the whole uptime when a sensor client is streaming.
+	 * Nothing is left to do here after the first handover, so disable
+	 * the interrupt until the next prepare() re-arms it.
+	 */
+	disable_irq_nosync(q6v5->handover_irq);
+
 	return IRQ_HANDLED;
 }
 
